  "locator": "I.9, 991a20–31",
  "interpretation": "Aristotle criticizes calling Forms paradigms and participation imitation without specifying what works by looking at them; resemblance can occur without copying, and the same thing may be paradigm and image. These are explanatory and likeness/copy challenges, not a derivation that every participation relation is resemblance or that every Platonism is contradictory. Bounded reading of the materialized Greek witness. Retained as prose; it is not silently equated with the stronger universal Lean reconstruction.",
